/**
 * Makes edits to local bit components hot-swap instead of reloading the page.
 *
 * babel already puts the react-refresh calls ($RefreshReg$/$RefreshSig$) into
 * these files. But each module must also be wired into the refresh runtime —
 * registered, and accepting its own hot updates. The refresh plugin's own
 * loader does that wiring, but it skips node_modules — and ALL bit components
 * live in node_modules. No wiring = every edit falls back to a full page
 * reload.
 *
 * So we add the wiring ourselves, for local bit components only
 * (`_bit_local: true`). Two loaders, because the glue must match the module
 * format:
 * - `.js` dist files are CJS → rspack's builtin loader is fine (its glue
 *   says `module.hot`, which exists in CJS).
 * - `.mdx`/`.md` compile to strict ESM → ESM has no `module`, so the builtin
 *   glue crashes with "module is not defined" on every mdx a preview loads
 *   (that bug shipped on main). Our own loader emits the same glue in
 *   ESM-legal form — see react-refresh-mdx-loader.cjs.
 */
